{
  "billId": 2146112,
  "billNumber": "S889",
  "title": "Property Tax Reappraisal Moratorium",
  "status": "4",
  "chamber": "S",
  "changeHash": "1b2bf8c2c4b2cb3ea0714c449739d535",
  "lastAction": "Ch. SL 2026-8",
  "lastActionDate": "2026-06-19",
  "url": "https://legiscan.com/NC/bill/S889/2025",
  "aiSummary": "This bill delays the use of new property values from 2026 reappraisals in counties with populations over 15,000 for the 2026-2027 tax year, requiring them to use the previous schedule of values instead. Starting in 2027-2028, counties will use the 2026 reappraisal values going forward. The bill also requires county assessors to pay a $20 examination fee to the Department of Revenue.",
  "aiProArguments": "Supporters argue this bill provides homeowners and businesses time to adjust to potentially significant property tax increases resulting from reappraisals without immediate financial shock. Proponents contend the one-year delay allows taxpayers to plan for higher tax bills and gives counties time to address concerns, while still implementing the new values fairly in subsequent years.",
  "aiConArguments": "Opponents argue the moratorium delays necessary tax system updates and creates inconsistency in property valuations, potentially causing fiscal uncertainty for county budgets that rely on accurate assessments. Critics contend the one-year delay shifts tax burdens to other taxpayers and may reduce tax revenue counties need for services, while the $20 assessor examination fee represents a minor additional cost that does not offset the larger fiscal impacts.",
  "topic": "Taxes & Budget",
  "textLength": 5329,
  "createdAt": "2026-06-23T03:11:36.241Z",
